TEXT 0 -232 Left 3 ;#90 LC ringdown
TEXT 0 -176 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=74fz9iwZ_sM
TEXT 0 -136 Left 2 ;A fast edge rings a parallel LC tank. Measuring the ring frequency with the capacitance known gives\nthe inductance, from L = 1 / ((2*pi*fR)^2 * C).
TEXT 840 96 Left 2 !.tran 0 10u 0 0.2n
TEXT 840 136 Left 2 !.save V(TANK)
TEXT 840 192 Left 2 !.meas tran TC1 WHEN V(TANK)=0 CROSS=4
TEXT 840 232 Left 2 !.meas tran TC2 WHEN V(TANK)=0 CROSS=6
TEXT 840 272 Left 2 !.meas tran RING_PERIOD PARAM TC2-TC1
TEXT 840 312 Left 2 !.meas tran RING_FREQ PARAM 1/(TC2-TC1)
TEXT 840 352 Left 2 !.meas tran FIRST_PEAK MAX V(TANK) FROM 100n TO 700n
TEXT 840 424 Left 2 ;CKNOWN is the 1 nF Alan picks as the known\ncapacitor, CCOUPLE the 10 pF he couples the\nfast edge through, and RPROBE the 10x scope\nprobe he clips on the tank. LUNKNOWN is the\npart being measured, shown here as 10 uH with\n8 ohm of series loss so the ring decays over a\nfew cycles as it does on his screen.
